# netsurf: Vita text drawn a run at a time
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# Hardware run 10: text-heavy pages cost 120-240 ms of CPU per frame, and
# every glyph was its own vita2d_draw_texture_tint_part() -- a vertex
# allocation and a GXM draw each. vita/text.c now collects a run's glyphs
# and draws them with one vita2d_draw_array_textured() per atlas page:
# triangle pairs with the same corners and texture coordinates as
# libvita2d's tint_part strip, so the pixels are the same. A run shares one
# colour, and blending two layers of one colour gives the same result in
# either order, so grouping by page cannot change overlaps. The glyphs'
# atlas rectangles are copied, not referenced: a later glyph of the run can
# take over a glyph_cache slot (the first cut drew a "9" as an "A").
# Simulator: ~15 glyphs per draw over the autotest; 68/68 frames pixel-
# identical to one draw per glyph (VITA_SIM_TEXT_UNBATCHED, the reference
# path the simulator keeps). font: log line with glyphs and draws.
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 14.

